    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Trans World Airlines",
      "COCKTAILS\nHeublein Manhattan Beefeater Martini\nHarveys Bristol Cream Sherry\nCampari\nScrewdriver\nMr. and Mrs. \"T\"® Bloody Mary\nSmirnoff Silver Vodka Martini\nBoccie Ball with Amaretto di Saronno,\nOrange Juice and Club Soda\nSPIRITS\nJack Daniels\nI.W. Harper\nSeagram's V.O.\nOld Grandad\nJohnnie Walker Red Label\nChivas Regal\nBeefeater Gin\nSmirnoff Silver Vodka\nBacardi Rum\nRemy Martin V.S.O.P. and Soda\nLIQUEURS\nRemy Martin V.S.O.P. Cognac\nAmaretto di Saronno\nCarolans Irish Cream\nThe above drinks are available at\n$2.50 each\nSelected Beers $1.50\nWINES \u0026 CHAMPAGNE\nTWA has selected these fine beverages.\nChampagne $3.50\nWine $2.50\nCHAMPAGNE\nLaurent Perrier\n1871\nTSTARUISHEN 1A1S\n•FRANC\nCORDIER\nSOAVE\nDENOMINAZIONE DI ORIGIN\nLE CONTROLLATA\nBOLLA\nMASSIC ZONE OF\nFRATELLI BOLLA S.P.A. - PRODUTTORI\nRESERVE\nLABOTTIERE\nBORDEAUX\nAPPELLATION BORDEAUX CONTROLEE\nDON ROOMINE\n1875d\nД Conde\nYour flight includes a selection from TWA's\nAmerican Harvest Service which features\nseasonal foods and regional cooking of the\nUnited States. We pay tribute to American\ncuisine by including some recipe ideas from\nTWA cities and from the American Harvest\nRestaurants in the Vista International Hotels.\nSALAD\nMarinated Garden Salad in Season.\nENTREE SELECTION\nFILET TIPS DIJONNAISE\nTidbits of Beef Tenderloin are Lightly\nSauteed then Blended in a Sauce of Beef\nStock, Herbs, Cream and a Touch of Dijon\nMustard. Served with Fresh Buttered\nFettuccine and Petits Pois.\nCHICKEN HARVESTER\nChicken Breast in a Cream Sauce\nwith Corn and Carrots.\nPresented with Rice and Green Beans.\nPlease accept our apologies if due to previous passenger\nselections, your entree preference is not available.\nDESSERT\nChocolate Mousse\nDinner Chocolate\nCOFFEE FLAVORS OF THE WORLD\n$2.50 Each\nMILANO with Amaretto di Saronno\nROYALE with Remy Martin V.S.O.P.\nCAROLANS IRISH\nTENNESSEE with Jack Daniels\nFROM TWA's RECIPE FILES\n8\nCHICKEN HARVESTER\nYield: 8 portions\nBoneless Breast of Chicken, Salt,\nWhite Pepper, Melted Butter\nSauce\n1-1 lb.\n1/2 cup\n. Can Creamed Corn\nHeavy Cream\nChicken Bouillon Cube\n2\n1 tbsp.\n1 pinch\n1 pinch\n1 pinch\n2 tsp.\nTo taste\nSmall Carrots Shredded\nCorn Starch dissolve with a little water\nGround Thyme\nGround Bay Leaves\nGround Sage\nParsley Flakes\nSalt and White Pepper\nPROCEDURE:\n1. Season chicken breast with salt and pepper; baste with\nmelted butter; place on buttered sheet pan; bake in\n350°F. preheated oven until done (baste frequently\nwith the dripping to avoid dryness).\n2.\nCombine all the sauce ingredients except cornstarch\n• mixture and the shredded carrots in a sauce pan.\n3. Bring to a boil over medium heat stirring occasional-\nly; simmer for 10 minutes.\n4. Add cornstarch mixture slowly to sauce pan, stirring\nconstantly. Bring back to a boil. Adjust seasoning\n5. Add half of the Shredded Carrots to the sauce; sim-\nmer for 3 minutes; remove from heat. Serve over\nChicken.\nBEVERAGES\nFreshly Brewed\nMAXWELL HOUSE® COFFEE\nFreeze-Dried\nSanka®\nSWEET'N LOWI\nLipton. rea\nMilk\nJuice\nCoca'Cola PEPSI-COLA\n7UP\ndiet Coke. diet pepsi@\ndiet\nCOUNTRY TIME®\nLEMONADE FLAVOR DRINK\nSoft drinks are with the Captain's\ncompliments.\nPRIOR TO ARRIVAL\nDevonshire Scone with Strawberry\nJam Clotted Cream and Apple Juice\nwill be served."
    ],
